    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Elevated blood pressure at intake (166/102 mmHg, average of two readings), first found at a workplace screening; ambulatory monitoring to confirm</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R03.0</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting finding, superseded by the confirmed diagnosis at two weeks.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Albumin in the urine (urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio 286 mg/g) with eGFR 54 by the race-free CKD-EPI 2021 equation; she recalls protein in the urine at an executive physical a year ago, and those records are requested; to be repeated and investigated</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R80.9</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting finding, superseded by the kidney diagnosis at two weeks.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Hypertension, stage 2, confirmed by 24-hour ambulatory monitoring (24-hour mean 149/94, daytime 154/98, night 140/88 without the normal nighttime fall), with left ventricular hypertrophy on ECG and mild hypertensive retinopathy; synthetic modern episode linked to her documented high blood pressure</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>I12.9</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis anchored to the documented hypertension and nephritis.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
